Editing the MPI Standard
========================
With the 3.0 Standard, there is now a document, instr.pdf (use make instr.pdf 
to create it) that describes the process of editing the document and approving 
changes.

Short version:
=============
make cleandoc - build the document
make allversions - build all versions, including ones with changes marked

LaTeX Issues
============
The changebar package must be version 3.5a or later to support color and 
pdflatex .

Updating the SVN tree
=====================
As of MPI 3.1, chapter authors will make changes directly into the
MPI-3.1 document.  Changes, especially minor changes, do *not* need to
be marked with change macros; many people, particularly those working
on the documents, felt that these made it harder to update and correct
the document, not easier.  Tools such as latexdiff can be used to show
changes; these are more reliable than manually entered change macros.

However, this does introduce a new problem, since svn does not have a
good "tag" mechanism (the svn approach is to create a copy, i.e., a
branch).  Since this is a version control system, all information is
in the logs, but to simplify creating consistent versions, please
update the REVISIONHISTORY file with major revision numbers.  That is,
if there is a version that should be considered a consistent and
complete working draft, include that in the REVISIONHISTORY file.

